WEBVTT

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.320
Big bro!

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.900
Gora-san!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.780
Gora-dono!

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:12.990
Yoo-hoo...

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.400
Doraemon...

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.530
Gora-san?

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.540
En-chan, what are you doing?

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.550
Oh, I thought it might 
have some sort of clue.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:32.570
Yeah, I'm lying.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.480
I just got curious.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.100
But look at this. It's Yumoto.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.760
Wow, he's tiny!

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.470
And Gora-san's so young!

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.050
What's all this?

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.460
Wow, you're right!

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.740
Yumoto hasn't changed at 
all! He's exactly the same!

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.190
And Gora-san looks like the 
quintessential big brother!

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.320
Senpai. You need to take looking 
for my brother seriously!

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.450
Sorry, sorry.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.420
This was all just so charming.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.040
What is it about other people's 
albums that's so fascinating?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:05.930
Hey!

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.790
What will happen to the Kurotama 
Bath if my brother disappears?!

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.800
What will I do?

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.540
If anything happens to my brother...

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.240
Don't you worry.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.850
He'll be back.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.240
Let us put our faith in Maximum Gorar!

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.360
He's a legendary hero, remember?

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.640
He'll be fine!

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.420
Big bro!

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.320
Come home!

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.770
Love is What Matters!

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.050
You're being transferred 
to the Andromeda branch?

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.130
Yeah.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.040
For three to five years.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:26.270
Is it a demotion?

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:28.500
They said it'll come
with a proper space wage.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.480
Will we have to change schools?

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.900
What about your promise to take 
us to Binan Land next month?

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.070
I'm sorry.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.470
But there'll be plenty of 
fun places in Andromeda.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.050
But is there Binan Land?!

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.220
We never even got to thank Gorar!

00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:00.980
I hate Andromeda!

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.820
<b>Space
School</b>

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.820
Earth?

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.160
Where's that?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.540
Gotta be out in the sticks, right?

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.590
Oh, I know.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.500
CIDE! That's where Gorar's from.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.310
You know Maximum Gorar?

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:12.960
Why?

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:16.540
That Gorar guy really gets under my skin.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.090
All he does is get in the way.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.840
Man, Earth sucks.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.570
I wish they'd bust it up soon.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.000
But they gotta get rid of Gorar first!

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.760
Gorar's just a big doo-doo head!

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.310
<b>Teacher's Office</b>

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:32.880
Picking a fight over some silly TV show?

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.580
<i>Gorar's not a bad guy...</i>

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.070
<i>Gorar's a hero!</i>

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.540
<b>Beppu Haruhiko               Beppu Akihiko</b>

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.790
This is stupid, right?

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.570
Yeah, it's stupid.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:05.740
Gora-san...

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.780
Gora-san...

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.970
Isn't Gora-san charming?

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.910
I want to tie him up and 
keep him beside me forever.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:16.470
I want to force a reluctant 
Gora-san to slap me.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.530
Tie him up?

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:19.400
You mean Gora-san?

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.110
Yeah.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.890
I don't want him running away.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.740
But... slap you?

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.130
You want Gora-san to do that?

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:26.780
Yeah.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.390
It sounds thrilling!

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.780
Aki, you've got weird tastes!

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.780
Haru, you've got strange tastes!

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.960
Gora-san...

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.790
...belongs to VEPPer forever!

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.550
Kinshiro, how far have you gotten in 
your Shakespeare research project?

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.720
I finished last week.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.180
Seriously?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.740
I'd better hurry, too.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.820
Mr. Chips is so strict.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.050
You're so lucky.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:56.730
I'm doing Latin grammar right now.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:57.890
It's such a bother.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:00.720
If you can learn Latin now, 
it will make things easier—

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.440
What's wrong?

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.560
My shoelace broke.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.400
Oh, dear...

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.540
Have you been looking after them?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.950
Of course.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.140
It's a bad omen.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.620
Hey, a black cat.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.510
Hey, cock robins.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.210
Something awful is about to happen.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.300
Really?

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.990
I think it's all in your head.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.320
Not to me.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.750
I feel like something bad's 
happening to At-chan.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:57.330
Really?

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:01.340
If it's so bad you can't even 
eat, why not send him an email?

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.350
To send him an email... 
for no particular reason?

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.720
Why not say, "Just felt like emailing 
you, no particular reason"?

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:09.340
What?

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.350
Can I do that?

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.750
Why not?

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.570
I'll email him, then.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.520
<b>Just felt like emailing you, no particular 
reason. How are things? -Kinshiro.</b>

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.070
<b>Sent</b>

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.030
<b>Kinugawa Atsushi</b>

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.030
<b>Cell Phone</b>

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.630
I hope he'll reply soon...

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:44.240
It's hard to relax without 
Gora-san's regular 'cha-chop'!

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.870
Truly, we're missing the finishing touch!

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.220
I wonder when he'll be back.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.840
If he's gotten mixed up 
with the Beppu Brothers...

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.210
I mean, VEPPer...

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:54.820
Yeah.

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.990
Maybe we should ask them directly?

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:58.560
That's tricky...

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:01.690
How'd it go?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.680
No use.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:04.480
Not a single sign of life.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.700
I told you not to turn it 
on until it dried fully.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:11.900
I thought it was! I used a hair dryer on it!

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:15.620
On the bright side, it didn't fall 
in after you'd done your business.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.500
I didn't think I was so 
dependent on my smartphone,

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.260
but now I know how Yumoto feels.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:27.090
You don't realize how important 
someone is until you lose them.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:31.260
You're equating Gora-san with a smartphone?

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.390
Kinugawa-senpai's so traumatized,

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.390
he's lost all his usual social graces.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.250
Yumoto forgot his cluelessness, too!

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.060
What was that?

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.730
Maximum Gorar is about to leave 
the Earth, never to return!

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:50.720
Gorar is a space legend.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.570
For the sake of his fans and 
supporters who respect that legend,

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:56.280
he's going to connect in 
friendship all over the cosmos

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.520
as an eternal member of VEPPer!

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:00.540
Heaven!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:01.970
Yeah, I lost the thread there.

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:04.690
All the English threw me off.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:09.290
In other words, they're taking Hakone Gora!

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.880
See you! Thank you! Bye!

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:31.800
What are you doing?

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.020
My office won't stand for this!

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:35.460
They're surprisingly flimsy.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:36.530
Yeah.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:39.790
They must get holes in them all the time.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:44.480
Just one poke from any slightly 
pointy household utensil...

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.250
Chopsticks, for example...

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.780
I-I-I'm sorry!

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.640
No need to apologize.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.270
So? Is Gora-san with them?

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:04.400
And they're going back 
into space with Gora-san?

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:08.430
So what about the fight they 
were trying to pick with us?

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:09.960
The original purpose of the fights

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:14.610
was to make it clear who 
was more worthy of Gora-san!

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:15.860
Really?

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:19.080
But they don't care anymore,

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.830
as long as Gora-san joins VEPPer!

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:27.870
<b>Hakone Gora
Born May 9th
Blood Type O  Taurus
Hobbies: Chopping Wood
Likes: His little brother</b>

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:33.640
Yeah, Gora really should 
be in the center, right?

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.530
Yeah.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:37.760
Speaking of which, it'll 
usually be the three of us,

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:43.390
but I was thinking of forming a new unit, 
just me and Gora, called "Go Lucky!"

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.480
Gora + Aki = Go Lucky! Get it?

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:46.910
What the heck?

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.440
That's not fair! I want a unit, too!

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.780
No!

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:52.170
If we try to sell another unit 
with the same name scheme,

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.700
it'll just dilute Gorar's value.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:55.320
Then...

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.450
Then I want Gorar to live in my room with me!

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:01.340
Huh? We have a guest room!

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:02.110
No!

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:04.390
Gorar will need a roommate to help him adjust

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:07.630
to his new life and take care of him!

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.860
Haru, you toss and turn in your sleep!

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.360
You'll keep Gorar up all night!

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.450
You <i>talk in your sleep</i>, Aki!

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.260
Ew.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.560
Give back my brother Gora!

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:30.340
Hakone Gora is Hakone Gora!

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:32.600
He's no more and no less!

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:35.320
My brother Gora should be my brother Gora!

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.490
We refuse.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.660
Hakone Gora's true form is Maximum Gorar.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:44.990
His deserves a position appropriate 
to his unparalleled charisma!

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:48.540
And what makes VEPPer so appropriate?

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.040
Let us tell you!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.500
Gorar is a hero!

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.130
VEPPer are idols!

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:55.960
It's a natural fit!

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:58.200
No, no. They're different.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.350
As different as gender-swap and BL.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:03.720
As different as compound and 
fixed interest over six months.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.680
Haru! Aki!

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.430
Hey, he peed—

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:11.980
We should leave this backwater planet 
behind and take off right now!

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:14.600
Are you... moist?

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.820
I need to talk to the promoters 
about the space concert tour!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.210
Better get going!

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.420
What's that? An earthquake?

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.080
No! This is...

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:29.700
The sound of space engines firing up!

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.880
Space engines?!

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.300
Yes, the rocket engines of a ship

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:37.130
that flies through space using highly 
advanced scientific technology!

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:42.380
I won't let Bro Gora go!

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:45.100
Yumoto!

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.930
Scarlet Love Lumiere!

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:48.930
Wait!

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.090
En-chan-senpai, why did you stop me?!

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.710
Calm down, Yumoto!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:01.390
We have a right to fight for Gora-san, too.

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:04.340
He's always been a good host 
to us at the Kurotama Bath.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:05.580
That's important.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:08.300
We're here with you, Yumoto.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:14.460
Everyone, for the sake of Gora-san, 
transform into the Battle Lovers!

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.520
This love-filled planet

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:18.420
will not abide those who lack love!

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:20.550
Those who wield loveless power

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.130
must kneel before love!

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.710
Love is power!

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:25.340
Love is hope!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.080
Be born for love!

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.810
Give your life for love!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:29.840
Love!

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:32.480
We are, forever, the heirs 
to the throne of love...

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.270
Battle Lovers!

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:36.140
Feel the power...

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:37.860
...of love!

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.790
Too late.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.000
You're the ones who said 
you didn't want to fight.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.310
You missed your chance.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:45.950
Dadacha, take us home.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.210
Well, you heard them.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:50.030
You'd better get going.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.370
If you don't,

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.330
I'll cast you into the vacuum of space!

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.830
I'm really mad about how right they are.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.630
Though, agitating someone as much as you can

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.410
then sweeping the rug out from under 
them is a pretty common tactic.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:04.340
The effectiveness of that tactic...

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.050
...is really getting under my skin.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.010
Please!

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.660
Fight us!

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:13.830
This is...

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:17.270
That legendary tactic, total forthrightness?!

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:20.050
To refuse such an honest plea

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:23.070
would disgrace you both as idols and heroes!

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.740
What will you do?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:25.780
A heartfelt gesture?

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:26.810
Cunning...

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:29.000
You must accept their offer!

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.230
That voice came from Gora-san...

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:33.880
Did he wake up?

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:35.160
And he wants them to accept?

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.740
You're...

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:41.340
Formerly head of TV Universe's programming 
production department, section 2,

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:43.380
currently assistant head clerk-in-training

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.670
at TV Universe's historical 
compilation office, copy division!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.130
Zundar!

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:48.700
Big bro!

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.000
Big bro?!

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.940
Dear little brother, Dadacha!

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:54.030
I'm glad you're doing well!

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:55.100
You too, big bro!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.580
I wasn't expecting you to 
show up at a time like this!

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.890
Fortunately, given my current 
position in the company,

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:04.290
it was easy to get vacation.

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:09.420
I got the box of detergents your 
ex-wife's family sent during Bon!

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.060
Did you?

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:14.140
I haven't heard anything 
from her lately at all...

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:17.410
I bet my nephews have all gotten big, too!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:20.160
Yeah, the child support's 
getting pretty rough.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:21.420
Huh?

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.860
Didn't Zundar get demoted?

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.920
And... they're brothers?

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.200
They're not even the same species!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:30.390
"Copy clerk" sounds like a demotion to me.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:35.220
No, my biggest concern is 
those serious family issues.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.160
Forget everything else!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.440
That's right!

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:41.440
Forget everything else!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:46.150
What happens here could 
decide the fate of Earth!

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:50.850
My beloved little brother and 
beloved Galaxy Idols, the VEPPer!

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:54.410
Now is the time for you to show 
your glory to the universe!

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:55.860
Dadacha.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:57.170
Who is this guy?

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.330
A porcupine?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.960
On one side, the ones who ruined my TV show, 
CIDE 2, and consigned it to the cancellation bin...

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.440
the Earth Defense Club!

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:07.800
The ones who had Chief Hireashi 
sent to the DVD pressing factory,

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:11.500
and I, Zundar, to a do-nothing 
job... the Battle Lovers!

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:15.380
And on the other side, the space idols 
with an album currently on sale,

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:16.480
the VEPPer!

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.100
What brings them together?

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.750
Maximum Gorar of CIDE 1!

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:23.200
It's a beyond-thrilling development!

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:23.950
Big bro!

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:25.860
You're wonderful! Huggles!

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:29.320
It's a little weird for him to label 
it "beyond-thrilling" himself.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.110
Well, that's TV people for you.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.440
This will bring big ratings for sure!

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:38.040
And this project will return me 
to the programming department!

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:42.120
Atsushi, tell him he's really counting 
his chickens before they hatch.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.550
No, he's really psyched himself up.

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:47.500
I would feel bad letting him 
know the real story now.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:50.630
I don't care about reasons or projects...

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:54.170
As long as you wake Bro Gora up safely!

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.650
This guy really does get under my skin.

00:15:57.650 --> 00:15:59.890
I'd love to see him cry.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.830
Good!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.020
Now's the time!

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:04.310
Three, two, one, cue!

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:17.990
<i>Ladies and gentlemen!</i>

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:21.080
<i>Welcome to the amazing show!</i>

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:24.210
This is Idol Battle!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.520
We're about to witness a 
fierce and beautiful battle

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:30.880
for the title of #1 idols on Earth!

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.540
Will it be VEPPer or the Battle Lovers?

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.720
You're the ones who will decide!

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:43.180
Please use the "Like" button 
on your remote control at home!

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.120
If the coin comes up Dadacha, 
VEPPer will go first!

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:53.070
If it comes up Wombat, the 
Battle Lovers will go first!

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:59.940
VEPPer goes first!

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:03.180
Don't you think it's strange, Atsushi?

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.360
How so?

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:07.170
In games, usually going second 
gives you the advantage, right?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:08.610
You're right!

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:10.460
Especially at music recitals 
and figure skating

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:13.570
and other performance-based competitions.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:18.560
But when they learned they were 
going first, they grinned.

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:28.480
Welcome to the VEPP theater!

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.990
I'm proud to introduce

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:35.610
that marvelous duo, the VEPPer!

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.420
Now's the time!

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:39.080
Enjoy the show!

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:50.380
<i>VEPPer, the twin stars 
racing through the galaxy!</i>

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.630
<i>Let's illuminate the mysteries 
of the universe...</i>

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.760
<i>On the name of the stars!</i>

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:10.110
<i>VEPPer, bringing a thrill 
to this blue planet!</i>

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:13.420
<i>Let's illuminate the entire world!</i>

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.550
The twin stars shining in the heavens!

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:16.830
<i>On the name of the stars!</i>

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:15.490
Salty Sol!

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:17.400
Melty Luna!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.740
Galaxy Idols, the VEPPer!

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:27.360
<i>There's a shining light</i>

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:30.780
<i>I won't let anyone else have</i>

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:33.720
<i>A pure, great revolution</i>

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:36.300
<i>Destiny! Fantasy! Galaxy!</i>

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:39.800
Like! Like! Like!

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:41.700
Like!

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.020
What's going on here?!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:52.770
The audience's "Likes" become 
attacks against their opponent!

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:56.030
A truly formidable advanced 
scientific technology...

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.980
There's too many!

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.280
Don't shave down our HP 
with these piddling things!

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.420
Maximum Gorar!

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:04.930
You were our light of hope!

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:06.550
We don't care if the Earth goes away!

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:08.770
As long as we have you, that's all we need!

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:11.080
Rather, we wish it <i>would</i> go away!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.140
Because then, we could be together forever!

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.740
A thrilling twist...

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:20.750
or rather, a stalkery one!

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:21.760
I can't move!

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:24.570
I didn't think they'd have a 
system like this in place...

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:27.720
It's wearing me down both 
emotionally and physically!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:28.820
My brother...

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:31.180
I know he's Earth's hero!

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:33.230
And I know that sometimes he would prioritize

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.800
being a hero over being my brother...

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.440
But... But...

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.700
I don't want to lose him 
to something like this!

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:45.180
The three of us will make 
a new world together!

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.240
And you can join us there!

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:10.390
VEPPer received a surge of likes!

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:11.380
Oh?

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:13.610
Have the Battle Lovers 
lost their will to fight?

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.760
If they don't stand up 
before the count of five,

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:17.410
they'll forfeit the competition,

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.670
and the VEPPer will win by default!

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:22.230
Five!

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:23.300
Four!

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:24.320
Three!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.570
Hold it!

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:31.740
Kin-chan?!

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:32.910
They surprised me.

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:33.770
What are they doing here?

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.250
That's right. What about your study abroad?

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:38.390
When you didn't respond to the email I sent,

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:39.900
I knew something was wrong.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:43.180
I've never had a faster trip home.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:46.930
You certainly are magnets 
for trouble, aren't you?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.400
What was that?

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:54.170
Well, well.

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:55.600
So you're not completely down!

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:58.460
And you three appear to 
have nothing better to do!

00:20:58.460 --> 00:20:59.180
So?

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:00.610
What's the show this time?

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:04.030
It's been some time, Caerula Adamas!

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.280
Zundar!

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:07.700
That's <i>Lord</i> Zundar, to you!

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:10.700
We are no longer

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:14.620
the kind of men who will follow you blindly.

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:17.680
Oh? You intend to defy me?

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:19.940
If following the path we have chosen

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:22.940
in a way you don't like 
is the same as defiance,

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:23.940
then let it be so!

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:28.180
Then prove to me that willingness 
with your own blood!

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:31.850
That's my big bro! Everything 
he says is so cool!

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:33.060
Yeah.

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:34.840
That <i>is</i> a more profound statement

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:38.260
than I'd expect from a papa 
porcupine with child support woes.

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:41.480
D-D-Do not speak of my children!

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:44.640
En-chan!

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:49.480
Conquest!

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:55.580
The Golden Chevalier, shining in radiance!

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:57.740
Aurite!

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:03.150
The Silver Chevalier, rustling young leaves!

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:04.840
Argent!

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:10.180
The Pearl Chevalier, making flowers bloom!

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:11.510
Perlite!

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:15.430
We are the rulers of this blue world...

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:17.270
Caerula Adamas!

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:58.770
Next Time

00:23:53.890 --> 00:23:58.770
Love Will Save the Earth!

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:57.030
Next time, 
"Love Will Save the Earth!"

00:23:57.030 --> 00:23:58.510
Love Making!
